  "rationale": "Multiple direct-match melanoma PRSs are present (e.g., PGS000079/118/732/743/766/790/813/002246/002247/002253/003430/004953/005208). Among these, PGS002247 is directly aligned to the target trait with a high-fidelity endpoint (\"Incident invasive melanoma\") and reports comparatively strong, PRS-relevant performance evidence in European evaluation (full_model AUROC 0.691; R² 0.072) without obvious heavy clinical covariate packaging (covariates: age, sex). Several alternatives are either (i) more covariate-heavy (e.g., PGS000743 includes many traditional risk factors), making their full-model AUROC less attributable to PRS, (ii) based on restricted/special populations (e.g., familial melanoma in PGS000813; childhood cancer survivors in PGS005208), or (iii) show weaker reported discrimination (e.g., many PRSweb melanoma models with AUROC ~0.58–0.62). Limitation: most candidates (including PGS002247) do not provide explicit PGS-only AUROC/R², so ranking relies on endpoint fidelity plus full-model metrics and study context; a near-tie exists with sibling PGS002246 (AUROC 0.688; R² 0.07) with very similar evidence."
}

