  "rationale": "Direct-match candidates are abundant (multiple models with trait_reported/trait_efo aligning to prostate cancer), but they vary in endpoint fidelity (e.g., aggressive/fatal/lethal/5-year risk/screening-packaged vs generic incidence/case-control) and many report only full-model metrics with non-comparable covariate sets. PGS001291 is a direct prostate cancer model with explicit PRS-only performance reported (PGS AUROC no covariates = 0.65437; PGS R2 no covariates = 0.03164), and its PRS-only R2 is plausibly below the provided heritability ceiling (h2_liability=0.1169), making the performance evidence interpretable. However, it comes from a pan-trait UK Biobank framework paper ('across 813 traits'), which domain knowledge flags as tending to generalize poorly relative to disease-focused multi-cohort scores; additionally, several disease-focused alternatives exist but lack directly comparable PRS-only metrics in the provided context, preventing a high-confidence best-in-class selection."
